/-!
# Collective Multi-Zero Pole–Repulsion Forcing Laws

Single-zero interior certificates hit a universal barrier (`MultiFrequencyCap`): for any finite
harmonic certificate, a single zero contributes effective weight `B < 2`, which certifies **zero**
interior width whenever the pole order satisfies `κ ≥ 2`.

This module establishes the coupled multi-channel interior forcing laws for a general
**completed positive system** (`CompletedPositiveSystem κ d F Λ`): a Dirichlet-type function `F`
nonvanishing on `Re s > 1` whose negative logarithmic derivative has even positive-definite height
sections `u ↦ Re(−F'/F)(σ + iu)` (`σ > 1`), together with an order-one entire completion
`Λ(s) = (s(s − 1))^κ Γ_ℝ(s)^d F(s)` satisfying `Λ(1 − s) = Λ(s)` and `Λ(s̄) = conj(Λ(s))`.

## Main results

1. **Orbit multiplicity extraction (`sum_orbit_resolvent_le_re_logDeriv`)**: for any `r` zeros
   `ρ₁, …, ρ_r` of `Λ` with pairwise distinct positive ordinates `Im ρ_ℓ > 0` and integer
   multiplicities `m_ℓ ≤ ord_{ρ_ℓ}(Λ)`, dihedral `{1 − ·, conj}` orbit disjointness inside the
   order-one Hadamard zero-pair series yields on `Re s > 1`
   `∑_ℓ m_ℓ (Re 1/(s − ρ_ℓ) + Re 1/(s − ρ̄_ℓ)) ≤ Re(Λ'/Λ)(s)`.
2. **Master coupled strip pole–zero forcing inequality (`coupled_strip_pole_zero_forcing`)**:
   evaluating multiplicative Gram positivity across any height tuple `x : Fin n → ℝ` and
   nonnegative channel amplitudes `c : Fin n → ℝ` at `s_{j,k} = (1 + δ) + i(x_j − x_k)` couples
   the collective zero resolvents directly against the pole budget `κ` and archimedean degree `d`.
3. **Sharp collective half-pole interior forcing (`collective_half_pole_interior_forcing`)**:
   via slow-doubling Følner Finsets in the height subgroup generated by `(Im ρ_1, …, Im ρ_r)` with
   no commensurability or separation assumptions, whenever `κ < 2 * ∑_ℓ m_ℓ`, at least one zero is
   forced strictly into the interior `Re ρ_ℓ ≤ 1 − w` (`w > 0`).
4. **Exact sharpness at `2M ≤ κ` (`exists_completedPositiveSystem_boundary_zeros_at_half_pole`)**:
   for every `r ∈ ℕ` and any `r` positive ordinates `γ_1, …, γ_r > 0`, twisting `ζ` by Laplace-positive
   boundary factors produces an explicit `CompletedPositiveSystem (2 * r + 1) 1 F Λ` with
   `Λ(1 + i γ_ℓ) = 0` for all `ℓ`, showing that `r = ⌊κ/2⌋` boundary zeros can sit on `Re s = 1`
   with zero interior depth.
5. **Uniform `(r + 1)`-channel star collar forcing and `κ²` collar sparsity
   (`collective_star_collar_forcing`, `card_separated_collar_zeros_le_sq_poleOrder`)**:
   coupling `0` against `r` `Δ`-separated ordinates in `[Δ, T]` with weights `(√r, 1, …, 1)` forces
   collective collar repulsion whenever `∑_ℓ m_ℓ > √r · κ`; setting `r = κ² + 1` bounds the number
   of `Δ`-separated zeros in the explicit `≍_{κ,Δ} 1/(d log(3 + T))` collar by `κ²`.
-/

